1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:17,435
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June fourteenth. In college baseball, the team from Kansai University won the national championship — their first title in fifty-four years. Let's listen.

2
00:00:18,036 --> 00:00:20,795
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:21,495 --> 00:00:30,952
[News] 6月14日、大学野球の日本一を決める大会の決勝が、東京でありました。

4
00:00:31,652 --> 00:00:38,564
[News] 決勝では、関西大学と慶応大学が対戦しました。

5
00:00:39,264 --> 00:00:45,024
[News] 試合は、関西大学が2対1で勝ちました。

6
00:00:45,723 --> 00:00:52,636
[News] 関西大学の優勝は、54年ぶりで、3回目です。

7
00:00:53,335 --> 00:01:00,776
[News] 関西大学は、4回に1点を取って、先に点を取りました。

8
00:01:01,475 --> 00:01:08,603
[News] 5回には、山本選手がホームランを打って、点を増やしました。

9
00:01:09,304 --> 00:01:17,415
[News] 先発の米澤投手は、5回を投げて、相手に点を与えませんでした。

10
00:01:18,115 --> 00:01:26,852
[News] 慶応大学は、8回に1点を返しましたが、最後まで追いつけませんでした。

11
00:01:27,552 --> 00:01:34,103
[News] 優勝した選手たちは、グラウンドでとても喜んでいました。

12
00:01:34,804 --> 00:01:36,436
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:37,036 --> 00:01:47,811
[Slow] 6月14日、大学野球の日本一を決める大会の決勝が、東京でありました。

14
00:01:48,611 --> 00:01:56,075
[Host] On June fourteenth, the final of the tournament that decides Japan's best college baseball team was held in Tokyo.

15
00:01:56,676 --> 00:01:59,028
[Vocab] 決勝

16
00:01:59,427 --> 00:02:07,828
[Host] It means the final — the last game that decides the winner. The first character means to decide, the second means victory.

17
00:02:08,427 --> 00:02:16,324
[Slow] 決勝では、関西大学と慶応大学が対戦しました。

18
00:02:17,123 --> 00:02:21,707
[Host] In the final, Kansai University faced Keio University.

19
00:02:22,307 --> 00:02:24,587
[Vocab] 対戦

20
00:02:24,987 --> 00:02:31,972
[Host] It means to face off, to compete against. You'll hear it for any match between two teams or players.

21
00:02:32,572 --> 00:02:39,147
[Slow] 試合は、関西大学が2対1で勝ちました。

22
00:02:39,948 --> 00:02:43,955
[Host] In the game, Kansai University won, two to one.

23
00:02:44,556 --> 00:02:46,788
[Vocab] 試合

24
00:02:47,187 --> 00:02:53,163
[Host] It means a game or a match. This is the everyday word for any sports contest.

25
00:02:53,764 --> 00:03:01,659
[Slow] 関西大学の優勝は、54年ぶりで、3回目です。

26
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:08,580
[Host] It was Kansai University's first championship in fifty-four years, and their third overall.

27
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:11,532
[Vocab] 優勝

28
00:03:11,931 --> 00:03:19,348
[Host] It means winning the championship — finishing first. The word literally combines being superior with victory.

29
00:03:19,948 --> 00:03:28,467
[Slow] 関西大学は、4回に1点を取って、先に点を取りました。

30
00:03:29,268 --> 00:03:33,924
[Host] Kansai University took one point in the fourth inning, scoring first.

31
00:03:34,524 --> 00:03:36,348
[Vocab] 点

32
00:03:36,747 --> 00:03:43,635
[Host] It means a point, or a score. To take a point is to score; you'll hear it in every sports report.

33
00:03:44,235 --> 00:03:52,372
[Slow] 5回には、山本選手がホームランを打って、点を増やしました。

34
00:03:53,171 --> 00:03:58,187
[Host] In the fifth inning, player Yamamoto hit a home run, adding to the score.

35
00:03:58,788 --> 00:04:01,044
[Vocab] 選手

36
00:04:01,443 --> 00:04:09,436
[Host] It means an athlete or a player. Add it after a name or sport to mean that player — useful all over sports news.

37
00:04:10,036 --> 00:04:19,324
[Slow] 先発の米澤投手は、5回を投げて、相手に点を与えませんでした。

38
00:04:20,124 --> 00:04:26,267
[Host] The starting pitcher, Yonezawa, pitched five innings and gave up no points to the other team.

39
00:04:26,867 --> 00:04:29,100
[Vocab] 投手

40
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:35,932
[Host] It means pitcher — the player who throws the ball in baseball. The first character means to throw.

41
00:04:36,531 --> 00:04:46,516
[Slow] 慶応大学は、8回に1点を返しましたが、最後まで追いつけませんでした。

42
00:04:47,315 --> 00:04:52,884
[Host] Keio University got one point back in the eighth inning, but couldn't catch up in the end.

43
00:04:53,483 --> 00:04:55,788
[Vocab] 追いつく

44
00:04:56,187 --> 00:05:03,004
[Host] It means to catch up, to draw level. Here, the team that was behind couldn't quite reach the other's score.

45
